  "summary_en": "EESC opinion welcoming the Commission's Apply AI Strategy while urging SME support, regulatory proportionality, a revised EU AI liability framework after the AI Liability Directive's withdrawal, social-partner involvement in governance, and funding in the 2028-2034 MFF. Includes brief sectoral comments on physical AI and robotics, defence and automated vehicles.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Calls for a revised, comprehensive EU AI liability framework after the AI Liability Directive's withdrawal.",
   "Urges formal involvement of social partners, civil society and SMEs in AI governance bodies (AI Office, observatory, board, Alliance).",
   "Calls for an EU framework on transparency and accountability in algorithmic management.",
   "Supports 'physical AI' and collaborative robotics focus but asks for more attention to labour market impacts.",
   "Asks for harmonised standards and certification for AI-powered vehicles and for IHL compliance in defence AI."
